## Invariants that results depend on

<!-- NUMBERED, because they get cited by number in commits and reviews. Each one is
     a property that must hold for the output to mean anything -- not a style
     preference. The test that pins each one goes in the same line where there is
     one; where there is not, say "not enforced" rather than leaving it ambiguous.

     Good invariants are falsifiable and surprising. "Code should be clean" is
     neither. "`package.server` must import without `package.ingest` being
     importable" is both, and names a containment boundary a reader would otherwise
     violate by tidying up an import. -->
1. <INVARIANT> — pinned by `<TEST>`.
2. <INVARIANT> — **not enforced**; <why, and what would enforce it>.

